---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

/**
 * The full-bleed band under a page's heading. Only `/synergates/eopyy` uses one.
 *
 * **Why it is full-bleed, having been tried contained.** The maintainer asked for two changes at
 * review: the title before the picture, and the picture contained rather than hero-like. The first
 * stuck. The second was built, measured and reverted, because the artwork cannot carry a narrow
 * column.
 *
 * It is not a geometry problem. Contained, the rendered ratio was 5.12 against the artwork's own
 * 5.12 at both 1440 and 390, so nothing was stretched. It is a scale problem: the ΕΟΠΥΥ lockup on
 * the right third carries a line of small caps reading `ΕΘΝΙΚΟΣ ΟΡΓΑΝΙΣΜΟΣ ΠΑΡΟΧΗΣ ΥΠΗΡΕΣΙΩΝ
 * ΥΓΕΙΑΣ`. Full-bleed at 1440 the band draws 1441px wide and picks the 1536w source, and that line
 * is legible. Capped at `medium` it drew 960px from the 1024w source, a third smaller in both
 * dimensions, and the line turned to mush. At 390 the contained strip was 68px tall and the whole
 * lockup was a smudge. A 5.13:1 banner with 6px caption text was drawn to be shown wide.
 *
 * Four properties reproduce the live rendering, each measured rather than eyeballed:
 *
 * 1. **`aspect-[34/7]`** is the live site's own box, 4.857 against the artwork's 5.128, so
 *    `object-cover` trims roughly 5% off the sides at every width. A different ratio is a
 *    different crop.
 * 2. **Full-bleed.** No `Container`, no gutter, so it must render as a direct child of `<main>`.
 * 3. **`bg-surface`.** The artwork is transparent through its middle and right third, and the
 *    legacy parent is `bg-white`. Our page ground is `--color-page` (`#f7f7f6`), so without an
 *    explicit white behind it the ΕΟΠΥΥ mark sits on grey and the blend falls apart.
 * 4. **`bg-brand/10` over the image**, the live `bg-primary/10` in the site's own teal. This wash
 *    is why the band reads pale teal rather than white, and it is the single easiest of the four
 *    to leave out by accident.
 *
 * The overlay is `pointer-events-none` so it cannot swallow a click, and the artwork carries no
 * text the page depends on, so nothing is read through the tint.
 */
interface Props {
  image: ImageMetadata;
  alt: string;
}

const { image, alt }: Props = Astro.props;
---

<div class="relative aspect-[34/7] w-full overflow-hidden bg-surface">
  {/*
    Eager and high priority: it is the largest thing near the top of its route and so the LCP
    candidate. `layout="none"` because the sizing is the aspect box's job, not the image's.
  */}
  <Image
    src={image}
    alt={alt}
    layout="none"
    widths={[640, 1024, 1536, 2000]}
    sizes="100vw"
    loading="eager"
    fetchpriority="high"
    decoding="async"
    class="size-full object-cover"
  />

  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 bg-brand/10"></div>
</div>
